    "stem": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Domestic rabbits vary in the length and colour of their fur.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Fig. 6.1 shows a domestic rabbit with short fur and a fur colour pattern called Himalayan.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "figure",
        "id": "fig6.1",
        "caption": "Fig. 6.1",
        "src": "figures/q6_fig6_1.png",
        "alt": "Domestic rabbit with short fur and the Himalayan fur colour pattern.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The two genes that determine the length and colour of the fur of this rabbit occur at the <b>A / a</b> locus and the <b>B / b<sup>h</sup> / b</b> locus. These two gene loci are on separate chromosomes.",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "items": [
          "The allele <b>A</b> results in short fur.",
          "The allele <b>a</b> results in long fur.",
          "<b>A</b> is dominant to <b>a</b>.",
          "The allele <b>B</b> results in black fur all over the body.",
          "The allele <b>b<sup>h</sup></b> results in black fur on the nose, ears, paws and tail of the rabbit, and white fur on the rest of the body (Himalayan pattern).",
          "The allele <b>b</b> results in white fur all over the body (albino).",
          "<b>B</b> is dominant to <b>b<sup>h</sup></b> and <b>b<sup>h</sup></b> is dominant to <b>b</b>."
        ],
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        }
      }
    ],
    "parts": [
      {
        "key": "a",
        "label": "(a)",
        "source": {
          "qp": 16
        },
